WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi! How are you?
-Good. How are you?

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good.
Congratulations.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.570 line:92%
Eight seasons of a sketch show

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
is impossible
with just two people.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you guys did it,
and the quality never dipped.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you change your approach
going into it

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
knowing this was your last
season as you were writing it?

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We tried not to
because I think, you know,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.418
you go in with the same mission,
which is to make something

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.186 line:92%
that's funny And relatable,

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gets to the heart
of an idea or a character.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.392
And you don't want to be overly
sentimental about something.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-'Cause I think that's

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bad place
from which to create,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're already
patting yourself on the back

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.464 line:92%
or you're running a victory lap.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that's not how
the audience is viewing it.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.535 size:81% position:41%
-No, but I will say,
as an audience member,

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm also very happy
to see the characters

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.939
that we've spent time with
over the last eight years.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
The feminist bookstore owners,
Toni and Candace, are back.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.080 size:84% position:42%
Was that -- Was it hard
to at least not feel

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little sentimental
when you knew you were playing

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.484 size:75% position:38%
characters like that
for the last time?

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I mean, for sure.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:56.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we've noted that the last
time you put on the wigs

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, you know,
with Lance, who's the --

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.527
-Yeah, Lance
is a personal favorite of mine,

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.227 line:92%
for those who don't know.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's Carrie as Lance.
-Yeah. So...

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the last time
I wore that mustache.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
and now I have that mustache,

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
just on a wall in my house.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, good.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:15.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really disgusting.
Yeah, no.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.342 size:75% position:38% line:92%
There was a sadness.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
And also sometimes
guests would come on the show,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they would be
sad in advance.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.184
You know, we would still
be weeks out of finishing,

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.552 line:92%
and they would get emotional.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that kind of amplified
our sense of sadness.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.557
So, yeah, the whole thing
has been very bittersweet.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:34.027 size:88% position:44%
-You directed multiple
episodes this year, yes?

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Does it -- do you feel --

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.897
Is the experience different?
I mean it must be different,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.500
but do you enjoy it more,
being on that side of it?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I enjoyed --
in the premiere episode,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.305 line:92%
which is tonight, actually.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.241
A huge portion of that episode,
I'm not in,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I enjoy,
and I tried to actually

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
direct the episodes
that are more Fred-focused.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. So that you don't
have to worry about

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
directing yourself
as a performer.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's a little tricky.
I lose perspective.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have to have
a lot of trust in the process

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in yourself,
and use playback,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.590 line:92%
and it's just a little clunkier.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:07.227
So I like when I can just watch
Fred and have some objectivity.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel as though every other
episode, every episode,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
you guys make an observation
or you play something

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I can't believe hasn't
happened to the degree

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:17.370 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that you guys do it.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys played podcasters
in the first episode.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just delightful.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you're
in the writer's room,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.345
do you have this moment of, "Oh,
this would be perfect for us

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play a couple
of super-dicky podcasters?"

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.048 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wouldn't say that
that was the exact quote...

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
...when we started writing it,
but I think we were

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking about how a podcast --
and I am a fan of them...

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am, too.
-...but they start to get

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:43.229
a little fetishistic, you know,
fetishizing the other.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:43.997 line:92%
Like, what would it be like

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
to live in a rural part
of the country?

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-"Well, I don't know.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people
live there already.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.703 line:92%
They could probably tell us."

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, just elevating
everything to this, you know,

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
really, like,
intense drama when --

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.646
It sometimes feels like they're
creating drama out of nothing.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.348
And so, yeah, we wanted
to explore that lovingly,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we take over
a police station.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it is very lovingly done.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is very clear
that you are people

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:11.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
who listen to
and enjoy podcasts, as well.

